Format: XML
Source: Third-party HTTP system

Key Fields:
BookingID
CustomerName
ReceiverName
ReceiverEmail
BookingDate, DeliveryDate
WaybillNumber, Destination, Quantity, Price, etc.

Output:
Format: HTML (Email body)
Target: Email client (via Mail adapter)
HTML includes a table with booking details.
Error Data:
Logged error message
MPL ID
Exception stack trace (if needed)
Optional: Failed payload (stored in Data Store or logged)

🔷 A – Application
Platform:
SAP Cloud Integration (SAP CPI)
Key Components Used:
HTTP Sender Adapter – receives XML from external system.
XSLT Mapping – transforms XML into HTML.
Content Modifier – for subject, recipient, and headers.
Mail Receiver Adapter – sends the HTML email.
Exception Subprocess – for error handling.
Groovy Script – for validations, logging, MPL ID capture.
Optional: Data Store / JMS Queue – for retry mechanism.

Dynamic Configuration:
Recipients and email subject derived from input payload.
Content-Type set as text/html using MIME-Type in Mail adapter.
HTML body passed via message body (as text or attachment).

